# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Node
node_modules/
web/dist/
*.local

# Pipeline scratch: raw simc output is huge and reproducible, only the
# distilled dataset under web/public/data is committed.
.work/
simc-bin/
*.simc.out
*.raw.json

# Probe output and response caches. A cache is what makes re-running the
# extraction free, and it is raw API payloads: large, and not ours to commit --
# `report.title`, `masterData.actors[].name` and the `name`/`guild`/`server`
# fields of every ranking row.
#
# `fight-probe/` was ignored and the other two were NOT, measured on 2026-09-12
# with `git check-ignore`. Nothing has been committed from them, and that is luck
# rather than design: the commit step of each workflow is scoped to
# `web/public/data`, so only a LOCAL run plus one `git add -A` was ever needed.
# Same reasoning as `/data/` below, and the same near-miss.
fight-probe/
spawn-probe/
harvest/
# Written at the repository root by `harvest-builds.yml`'s probe step.
harvest-report.txt

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local screenshot helper (see CLAUDE.md); not part of the app
web/shot.mjs

# Git worktrees created for parallel agent runs. Tooling state, not project content.
.claude/worktrees/

# Screenshot output from the local helper above.
web/shots*/

# The private cohort data repository, checked out here by progress-sweep.yml and
# written by `wowdps progress-sweep --out data/progress-cohort`. It holds guild
# names, realms, hours and first kills -- the rows this repository exists to keep
# OUT of a public history. A local run leaves them here, and one `git add -A`
# would commit them irreversibly.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `data/` matches any directory of that
# name at any depth, which would silently ignore `web/public/data/` (the published
# dataset) and `pipeline/src/wowdps/data/` (gear_pools.json).
/data/
